:0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":30,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the plan for CAT-01 to `tasks/CAT-01/plan.md`, replacing the earlier plan file there. The story is an adoption: it describes behaviour the shop already has, so the plan builds nothing and changes no existing test.\n\n**All five scenarios are in the code** (Product context, `GET /products`):\n- **21 cards:** the seeder creates 21 products (`SampleDataSeeder.cs:25-49`), and `Catalog.cshtml` renders one card per product.\n- **Name order:** the product list is sorted by name, character by character (`InMemoryProductRepository.cs:53`). `\"Bounded Context\" Enamel Pin` comes first because a quote mark sorts before letters.\n- **Card contents and \"View Details\" link:** `Catalog.cshtml:16-29` and `:41`.\n- **Title, heading, breadcrumb:** `Catalog.cshtml:2-8`. The \"Product Catalog\" title is not committed yet. It is the catalogue-title story's change, and that story is still waiting on your answer to decision `catalogue-title-01`. CAT-01 can only be adopted once catalogue-title is delivered. The plan cites your answer to CAT-01-01 (option 2) for this.\n\n**Test levels and coverage:**\n- **Happy path (browser test):** already covered by `SeededCatalogE2eTest`.\n- **Name order:** covered by that browser test and by a unit test, but no integration test checks it through the page.\n- **Card shows name, description and image:** no test at all. `ProductPageTest` checks the same image and description on the product page, not on the card.\n- **\"View Details\" on every card:** only partly covered. Two tests follow one card's link; none checks every card or the link text.\n- **Title and breadcrumb:** only catalogue-title's browser test checks them; the heading is also checked by two integration tests.\n\nThe test stage will need to write new integration tests for these gaps.\n\n**Also in the plan:**\n- Two proposed glossary terms: \"Catalogue page\" and \"Product card\".\n- `seed-catalogue.json` is not in this repository; it lives in the separate, unpublished specification repo. The plan assumes it holds the same 21 products as the seeder.\n- The uncommitted `ProductPageTest.cs` and `ProductPageE2eTest.cs` belong to CAT-02, so the plan lists them as partial coverage only.\n\nNo question needed your decision, so there is no new decision record. I ran no other stage.","ttft_ms":4632,"type":"result","duration_ms":109367,"uuid":"30d6cd24-52a5-4c48-b1cf-793a026bf91b","ttft_stream_ms":3782,"time_to_request_ms":211,"first_content_frame_ms":3782,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
